      "id": 1,
      "text": "Cheviot was laid out on March 21, 1818, and named after the Cheviot Hills in southern Scotland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheviot%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "John Craig, a Scottish immigrant, bought 320 acres in 1818 and founded the town that would become Cheviot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheviot%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town grew around an inn and tavern on the Harrison Pike, where Craig sold lots and encouraged settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheviot%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cheviot incorporated as a village in 1901 and later became a city in 1931.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheviot%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
